%% Support access, operations health, reconciliation, and audit evidence
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant Operator as Platform operator
    participant Console as Operations console
    participant API as Platform API
    participant Support as SupportAccessService
    participant Health as OperationsHealthService
    participant Recon as Usage/reconciliation service
    participant DB as Control and tenant databases
    participant Audit as Platform and tenant audit

    Operator->>Console: Request tenant support access
    Console->>API: Submit organization, reason, scope, expiry
    API->>Support: Validate permission and required reason
    Support->>DB: Create time-bounded support grant
    Support->>Audit: Record actor, target, scope, and expiry
    API-->>Console: Sanitized grant status

    Operator->>Console: Open tenant support session
    Console->>API: Present active support grant
    API->>Support: Verify scope, expiry, and revocation
    Support-->>Console: Allowed read/support context
    Console->>DB: Read only permitted tenant data
    Console->>Audit: Record support action and correlation ID

    Operator->>Console: Open health dashboard
    Console->>API: GET database/domain/system health
    API->>Health: Probe control plane, tenant readiness, Redis, queues, providers
    Health->>DB: Run bounded dependency checks
    DB-->>Health: Health evidence
    Health-->>Console: HEALTHY, DEGRADED, or UNAVAILABLE signals

    Operator->>Console: Reconcile usage or financial finding
    Console->>API: Start bounded reconciliation
    API->>Recon: Compare authoritative tenant facts to recorded counters/findings
    Recon->>DB: Read facts and persist correction/finding
    Recon->>Audit: Record reconciliation actor and outcome
    API-->>Console: Evidence and next action

    Note over Support,Audit: Support access is explicit, scoped, time-bounded, revocable, and audited.
    Note over Health,DB: Health output is an operational signal, not proof of global capacity or production readiness.
